    "narrative": "With the league calendar reaching late October, the Austin Waves remain in a holding pattern as the majority of our core is currently inactive. Today\u2019s actionable intelligence is limited, as the primary offensive engine\u2014anchored by **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**\u2014is sidelined due to scheduled off-days. Consequently, **Liam Hicks** stands as our singular active consideration. With a projected score of 41.38, he sits squarely in the marginal tier, largely buoyed by a projected cleanup spot in the order. While we lack the high-leverage stolen base threat typically provided by **Luis Robert Jr.** or **Nasim Nunez** today, the optimizer suggests holding **Liam Hicks** in the lineup if games-played caps allow, as the projected volume at #4 in the order slightly offsets the lack of an elite matchup profile.\n\nThe bench remains crowded with high-upside assets who would typically be forced into the rotation if not for today\u2019s scheduling drought. **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jordan Westburg** are all currently restricted by the team's off-day status, effectively neutralizing the speed-driven production we usually rely on from the likes of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Sam Antonacci**. We are monitoring the status of **Drake Baldwin**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Miguel Vargas**, and **Josh Jung** for potential late-week surges, but as it stands, no player has cleared the 60-point threshold required to warrant an aggressive start. Defensive depth pieces such as **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Franklin Arias** remain on standby, though their usage remains strictly capped until a more favorable pitching environment manifests.",
